# Check findings are work

A diagnostic from ruff, Biome, pytest, or `pnpm build` is a defect in this cycle, not a note for later. Do not leave a known failure, skip it with `--no-verify`, or paste the output and move on.

## Apply the suggestion when it is the fix

If the tool marks the finding as auto-fixable (`[*]`, `FIXABLE`, `ruff check --fix`, `biome check --write`), apply that fix. Then re-run the same check.

```bash
# ❌ BAD — report I001 / format drift and continue
uv run ruff check src tests
# "19 files would be reformatted"

# ✅ GOOD — apply, then prove it is clean
uv run ruff check --fix src tests
uv run ruff format src tests
uv run ruff check src tests && uv run ruff format --check src tests
```

Frontend: `pnpm format` (Biome `--write`), then `pnpm lint`.

## Inspect what the fixer cannot touch

Line length, logic, type errors, and failing tests need a real edit that matches the surrounding code — wrap, rename, or rewrite; do not `# noqa` or disable the rule to get a green run.

```python
# ❌ BAD — silence E501
raise ValidationError(f"metric {metric.slug!r} does not belong to the goal's area")  # noqa: E501

# ✅ GOOD — wrap to line-length 100, same wording
raise ValidationError(
    f"metric {metric.slug!r} does not belong to the goal's area"
)
```

Re-run the failing check after the edit. The cycle is done only when the gate is green.
